Atlas overlay patch 0072: ui/webui-tokens
Why: the internal pages of the engine (settings, history, downloads) follow the WolOS tokens (the type is Inter first, the system font after it): the accent as the fallback of the primary colour before the colour sheet loads, the radii and the type variables, and the button radius (8). The colours themselves reach these pages through the browser's colour provider (patch 0070), so only what that does not carry is here. The block between the markers is generated by atlas/transform/tokens.py from the design repo's tokens/colors.json and is never edited by hand (`tokens.py --check` fails on drift).
Files: ui/base/webui/web_ui_util.cc, ui/webui/resources/cr_elements/cr_shared_vars.css, ui/webui/resources/cr_elements/cr_button/cr_button.css
Test filter: python3 -I atlas/transform/tokens.py --check DESIGN_REPO
Rebase risk: L (a block added above an existing rule, and two values)
Release: 0.13
License: GPL-3.0-or-later (hunks in files the inherited series touches or adds)
Verified at: 156.0.8078.79, prepared tree with the inherited and platform series applied

